        "body": "Stack 4 of 4. Depends on #103604.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Matrix QA migration still leaves a temporary compatibility plugin, private\nruntime facade, package/build inventory entries, and a separate documentation\nsurface after QA Lab has become the canonical scenario and workflow owner.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMove the `qa matrix` CLI registration and its deterministic native-handle exit\nguard into QA Lab, then delete the temporary plugin and transient runtime\nsurface. Consolidate the operator reference into the QA overview and remove the\ndeleted package from build, package, discovery, and generated inventories.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMaintainers keep the same eight Matrix profiles, 92 default scenarios, explicit\nscenario selection, Docker-backed transport behavior, and standard QA artifacts\nthrough one permanent QA Lab owner. Source builds and packaged inventories no\nlonger carry the temporary `qa-matrix` package.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm openclaw qa matrix --profile release --provider-mode mock-openai\n  --fail-fast`: both release scenarios passed against a disposable Tuwunel\n  homeserver, all three standard artifacts were written, and the direct QA Lab\n  command exited successfully on Blacksmith Testbox\n  `tbx_01kx5mgn8jwgz9a3skm5e2g4gn`.\n- Focused Testbox suites passed for the QA Lab CLI/runtime, plugin SDK and\n  discovery, package inventory, bundled build entries, runtime postbuild, and\n  plugin gateway gauntlet (including 12 Matrix CLI/runtime tests, 29 postbuild\n  tests, and 59 gauntlet tests).\n- `pnpm check:docs` passed Markdown formatting/lint, MDX, internal links, and\n  generated docs-map checks.\n- `pnpm build` passed after exercising the staged-deletion build and postbuild\n  paths.\n- Fresh autoreview found the missing Matrix native-handle termination guard; it\n  was moved into QA Lab with success, failure, exit-code, and opt-out coverage.\n  The post-fix autoreview completed clean with no accepted/actionable findings.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n",
